  <h2>Scaling Your Brand: Choosing the Right Production Partner</h2>
  <p>One of the most critical decisions for a fitness brand founder is deciding how much control they need over the design process versus how fast they want to launch. Understanding the difference between <strong>OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturing)</strong> and <strong>ODM (Original Design Manufacturing)</strong> is key to optimizing your supply chain.</p>
  
  <h3>OEM: For the Precise Visionary</h3>
  <p>In the OEM model, the brand provides the technical packs, fabric specifications, and exact designs. <strong>FITCLO</strong> acts as your manufacturing arm, executing your vision with precision. This is ideal for established brands with a dedicated design team looking for high-capacity, high-quality execution.</p>

  <h3>ODM: For Rapid Brand Growth</h3>
  <p>ODM allows you to select from our pre-designed, factory-tested styles and customize them with your branding (Private Labeling). This model significantly reduces lead times and development costs, making it the perfect choice for startups or brands looking to test new market trends quickly.</p>

  <h3>Which One Fits You?</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4 my-6 text-gray-700">
    <li><strong>Choose OEM if:</strong> You have unique, patented designs and need full control over every stitch and seam.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose ODM if:</strong> You want to launch a professional collection in 4-6 weeks using proven, high-performance silhouettes.</li>
  </ul>

